.TH strchrnul 3 2026\-02\-25 "Linux man\-pages (未リリース)" 
.SH 名前
strchrnul \- string search character or NUL
.SH ライブラリ
標準 C ライブラリ (\fIlibc\fP,\~\fI\-lc\fP)
.SH 書式
.nf
\fB#define _GNU_SOURCE\fP  /* See feature_test_macros(7) */
\fB#include <string.h>\fP
.P
\fBchar *strchrnul(const char *\fP\fIs\fP\fB, int \fP\fIc\fP\fB);\fP
.fi
.SH 説明
The \fBstrchrnul\fP()  function is like \fBstrchr\fP(3)  except that if \fIc\fP is
not found in \fIs\fP, then it returns a pointer to the null byte at the end of
\fIs\fP.
.P
It is equivalent to both of the following expressions:
.P
.in +4n
.EX
strchr(s, c) ?: strnul(s)
s + strcspn(s, (char [2]){c, \[aq]\[rs]0\[aq]})
.EE
.in
.SH 返り値
The \fBstrchrnul\fP()  function returns a pointer to the matched character, or
a pointer to the null byte at the end of \fIs\fP if the character is not found.
.SH 属性
この節で使用されている用語の説明については、 \fBattributes\fP(7) を参照。
